# The containers' slice in the Guest Image's Docker image
# (guest/rootfs-docker/configure.sh): containerd, Docker Engine and every
# container, through Docker Engine's cgroup-parent. Under memory pressure
# the kernel reclaims and kills here first, below the MicroVM's memory, so
# the guest agent keeps running.
#
# The IO limits cap the containers' block I/O on the root filesystem's
# device, so that a container cannot keep the MicroVM's block queue full.
# Firecracker serves the block device and the vsock from one thread, and
# a full queue holds the guest agent's heartbeats back until flintlock
# drops the exec stream (#133). The numbers are below a gp3 EBS volume's
# baseline of 3,000 IOPS and 125 MB/s. systemd resolves `/` to the block
# device under the root filesystem when it applies the limits, so the
# device's name does not matter: /dev/vda under Firecracker and Cloud
# Hypervisor alike. /etc/default/flr-io raises or removes a limit, through
# the flr-io generator (GI-072). Stage scripts run in agent.slice and are
# not limited.
[Unit]
Description=Docker Engine, containerd and their containers

[Slice]
MemoryMax=90%
CPUWeight=100
IOReadIOPSMax=/ 1500
IOWriteIOPSMax=/ 1500
IOReadBandwidthMax=/ 60M
IOWriteBandwidthMax=/ 60M
